bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    rt_process_is_running_lane_drift_non_child_pid_2026-11-26, 3, "2026-11-27 opus-bugbatch: fixed. env_process.rs rt_process_is_running falls back to the existing process_exists_os(pid) (kill(pid,0)/EPERM, OpenProcess on Windows) for a pid absent from SPAWNED_CHILDREN; tracked children still answer by try_wait. Red->green: new runtime unit test test_process_is_running_probes_os_for_untracked_pid failed at the getpid assert, now passes (cargo test -p simple-runtime --lib process: 65 passed). Seed JIT probe (std.io_runtime getpid/process_is_running): base c6f98def228712ea self=false init=false bogus=false; fixed seed 5347b0437924bb29 self=true init=true bogus=false, matching the interpreter. Perf: one kill(2) on the untracked path only."
    rt_process_is_running_lane_drift_non_child_pid_2026-11-26, 0, "Evidence is seed-JIT only. Measured on release/1.0.0 c917ac12f15, seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b sha256 fb80903917d6d5f5, with a 6-line program calling std process_is_running: compiled by the seed JIT getpid()->false and pid 1->false; SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter getpid()->true and pid 1->true; 999999999->false in both. No natively linked binary (C runtime lane) was run."
    rt_process_is_running_lane_drift_non_child_pid_2026-11-26, 1, "The outlier is the Rust runtime twin, src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/value/sffi/env_process.rs:1269: it consults only SPAWNED_CHILDREN and returns false for any pid absent from it. The interpreter (src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/interpreter_extern/system.rs:1415-1426) deliberately falls back to an OS liveness probe for a pid it did not spawn; that was the fix for interpreter_process_is_running_false_for_unspawned_pid_2026-09-06 (caret roster showed every agent as exited). The C runtime (src/runtime/runtime_process.c:112-125) does the same: waitpid, then kill(pid, 0) on ECHILD."
    rt_process_is_running_lane_drift_non_child_pid_2026-11-26, 2, "Proposed fix: make the Rust runtime twin match the other two lanes, i.e. on a pid absent from SPAWNED_CHILDREN return process_exists_os(pid) (the helper already sits directly below it at env_process.rs:1285) instead of false. Needs a Rust test for a live non-child pid and a seed redeploy. Effect seen before the caller was changed: the WM remote-app host refused every surface-open with bad-pid when compiled by the seed JIT while passing every interpreted spec; that caller now uses process_exists."

